                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "1. This is incredibly amateurish; it has a very \"baby's first Unity project\" feel to it.\n\n2. Controls are ass-backwards and terrible. Trigger to teleport, touchpad to grab? WTF?\n\n3. Worst of all, it doesn't \"quit\" when you quit; you have to go to it on desktop to close it, and it even manages to make it so you can't do that in Steam's virtual desktop, either. It's still running in the backgruond until you take off your headset and physically Ctrl-Alt-Del to kill the process.\n\nDon't waste your time.\n\nIf you're wondering why there are no other reviews of this, it's because you have to have played the game at least five minutes to leave a review, and it takes about a minute and a half to write it off completely. I opened it again just to have enough playtime to leave a review. You're welcome, Internet.",
